## The Real Problems DebugAid Should Solve

DebugAid should focus on expensive debugging tasks, not trivial ones.

### High-value problems

- "Why did this target fail to compile even though the header exists?"
- "Where is this unresolved symbol declared, defined, and why is it not linked?"
- "This crash happened here, but which earlier frame likely introduced the bad state?"
- "This sanitizer trace points to frame 0, but where is the actual ownership bug?"
- "This CI log is thousands of lines long; what are the 5 lines that matter?"
- "I am new to this subsystem; what code and build targets actually own this failure?"
- "Which file or target probably caused this regression?"
- "Why does this build work in one target/configuration but fail in another?"

### Problems that are not enough by themselves

- finding a file when the compiler already prints the exact file path
- generic code chat with little build or repo context
- broad semantic search without debugging-specific reasoning

Those can exist as supporting features, but they should not define the product.

