## What Makes the Product Special

DebugAid should feel different from a generic assistant in these ways:

### Repo-aware

It should know the actual indexed repo, not just the text the user pasted.

### Build-aware

It should understand that many C++ failures are caused by target wiring, include paths, compile flags, generated code, and library edges, not only by code inside one file.

### Failure-specific

A linker analyzer should behave differently from a segfault analyzer.

### Evidence-backed

The LLM should summarize evidence, not invent retrieval or diagnosis from scratch.

### Practical for private code

The default design should remain local-first and cheap to run.

