## Technology Strategy

### Keep using

- Python for orchestration and product velocity
- Tree-sitter for broad source parsing
- BM25 for strong lexical/symbol retrieval
- vector retrieval for semantic support
- local on-disk indices for cheap operation

### Add next

- stronger CMake/build graph understanding
- `compile_commands.json` as first-class input
- richer symbol ownership and declaration/definition mapping
- persistent session or daemon mode for faster repeated queries

### Add later

- libclang or clangd-backed semantic analysis for higher-fidelity C++ understanding
- learned reranker trained on log-code candidate pairs
- profiler/sanitizer-specific ingestion
- editor or CI integrations

### Cost discipline

The expensive part should not be an always-on hosted LLM.

The system should do most of its real work through deterministic local analysis, and use an LLM only when it adds explanation quality.

