## Product Roadmap

## Phase 1 - Retrieval Foundation

Goal:

- turn logs into relevant candidate files/functions reliably

Delivered:

- indexing
- log parsing
- hybrid retrieval
- strict pathless evaluation
- ablation harness

Completion standard:

- good retrieval quality on synthetic and pathless benchmarks
- enough parser coverage to support real Phase 2 diagnosis

## Phase 2 - Failure Triage Product

Goal:

- make the tool genuinely useful for live build/debug workflows

Core deliverables:

- `watch` mode
- structured diagnosis output
- compile command ingestion
- linker declaration/definition reasoning
- build-target inference
- CMake target/link analysis
- real-dataset evaluation on GitHub-mined samples

Success criteria:

- useful diagnosis on real compiler/linker/build failures
- stable CLI workflow for live triage
- no major regression in retrieval quality

## Phase 3 - Runtime and Memory Debugging Assistant

Goal:

- help with crashes and ownership/lifetime debugging, not just build failures

Core deliverables:

- deeper stack-trace reasoning
- ASan/UBSan-specific analyzers
- caller-context retrieval
- ownership and bounds heuristics
- better runtime exception triage

Success criteria:

- meaningful help on segfaults and sanitizer logs
- identifies likely bad-state introduction sites, not just crash sites

## Phase 4 - Performance and Optimization Assistant

Goal:

- become useful for performance triage and code-health diagnosis

Core deliverables:

- profiler ingestion
- hotspot explanation
- allocation and copy/move heuristics
- lock/synchronization hotspot analysis
- benchmark regression summaries

Success criteria:

- practical value on profiler/benchmark outputs
- evidence-backed optimization suggestions

## Phase 5 - Interactive Repo Intelligence

Goal:

- become a broader debugging and code-understanding assistant for large repos

Core deliverables:

- explain mode
- subsystem ownership summaries
- richer call/symbol graph exploration
- CI comment generation
- optional editor integration

