## Evaluation Strategy

We should measure what matters, not only what is easy.

### Retrieval metrics

- R@1, R@3, R@5
- MRR
- strict pathless slices
- real GitHub-mined slices

### Diagnosis metrics

- correct failure type
- correct likely cause family
- correct primary file or target
- correct declaration/definition pairing
- useful next-step suggestion

### Product metrics

- time to first useful answer
- repeated-query latency
- index build time
- memory footprint
- usefulness on unfamiliar repos

### Dataset priorities

- synthetic evaluation remains useful for controlled coverage
- real mined issues are more important for honesty
- pathless cases are the most important benchmark for real product value

