## What "Amazing" Actually Means for This Project

An amazing version of DebugAid is not one that does everything.

It is one that developers trust during stressful debugging because it is:

- fast enough to use in the loop
- accurate enough to not waste their time
- honest about confidence
- grounded in repo and build evidence
- able to solve failures that grep and a generic LLM do not solve cleanly

If a developer can run:

```bash
debugaid watch --repo ./repo --build-dir ./build -- ninja -j8
```

and get back:

- the likely broken target
- the declaration/definition pair
- the missing include or link edge
- the likely root cause
- the next thing to edit

then this project is genuinely strong.

